 "kind": "A design-stage check on the laptop's GPU, not pre-registered: one seed, the first 2,250 updates of the test bed's 24,000-update schedule. It decides which gate laws are stable enough to screen, and nothing about their worth.",
 "why": "The gated laptop arm of gated_cells_with_data trails the plain bed by 0.108 at 24,000 updates. Two measurements of that arm pointed at causes a cell could change. Its gate dendrites' fine spikes counted as pulses and took 22% of the stack's (23,013 of 103,672 a byte in windows at 24,000 updates), so the state reads lost 30% of their spikes and the output 16% against the plain base. And an open shunting gate let in 80% to 94% of the value dendrite's charge, close to an on/off switch. Commit 26198b3 added two options: --granule-inner-gate, whose gate steps stay inside the cell as dendritic steps that send no pulse, and --granule-ramp T, a proportional gate: the gate fires 4 steps for every threshold of its charge above the rest, and k steps let in k / (4T) of the value's charge, so every step lets in the same share, up to the whole charge at T thresholds and never more. Under the bounded pool a ramp divides by the gate's present largest count instead, which falls as the pool raises the threshold.",
